# `STATECHART-GENRE-SCOPE`: this fixture read `figdown 0.2 block` until the language
# number moved and `0.2` became a version the engine accepts. Its SUBJECT is
# unchanged — an unknown MINOR version is a line error, not a lenient parse
# (`UNKNOWN-MINOR-VERSION`) — so the fixture keeps its name and its citation, and moves to the
# next minor the engine does not implement.
# `DRAWN-ANNOTATION-FORM`: the same thing happened again. `note=` made the language
# number move 0.2 → 0.3 (core §13.0: a new option key is a new feature of the
# document format, so it cannot ship under a `Z` bump), `0.3` joined
# LANG_VERSIONS, and this fixture moved on to `0.4` by the same rule. Expect
# this line to move once per `Y` bump for as long as the fixture exists; that
# is the fixture working, not rotting.
# `SEQUENCE-GENRE-VOCABULARY`: and again. The `sequence` genre token is language
# surface, so it moved the language number 0.3 → 0.4 by the same core §13.0
# rule, `0.4` joined LANG_VERSIONS, and this fixture moved on to `0.5`.
figdown 0.5 block
node a "A"
